  "format": "Mitsubishi GX Works3 program export to CSV (instruction list, UTF-16 LE, tab-delimited) + device comment CSV",
  "machine": "Single-head inline bottle capper. Bottles arrive on a conveyor and are held at the capping station by a stop gate. When a bottle has settled (0.5 s) and a cap is in the chuck with the head up, the bottle is clamped, the pneumatic head lowers and the spindle motor screws the cap on until the torque clutch switch makes. After a 0.3 s dwell the head rises, the clamp opens, good bottles are counted against the batch size in D0 (500) and the gate releases the bottle while the escapement feeds the next cap. If torque is not reached within 3 s the bottle is marked as a reject and pushed off on release; 5 rejects stop the machine. A maintenance pushbutton jogs the spindle when the machine is not running.",
  "plc": {
    "brand": "Mitsubishi Electric",
    "family": "MELSEC iQ-F",
    "cpu": "FX5U-32MT/ES",
    "software": "GX Works3",
